<title>SWITZERLAND: Opel/Vauxhall 1996 profit falls 2.3 pct - GM.</title>
<headline>Opel/Vauxhall 1996 profit falls 2.3 pct - GM.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Motors Europe, the international division of the U.S. automotive group, said the 1996 net profit of Opel/Vauxhall eased to $778 million from 1995's $796 million.</p>
<p>GM Europe also said in a statement released from its Zurich headquarters that GM's International Operations (outside the U.S., Canada and Mexico) had 1996 sales of $35.25 billion and net profit of $1.53 billion.</p>
</text>
